  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1222 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nAn inverted trough currently located over the northwest Gulf will \ncontinue to usher in a northerly breeze as it progresses \nsoutheastward across the Gulf into Thursday. A cold front is set to \narrive Thursday afternoon which will clear skies and lower humidity \nwith highs in the lower 70s across the area. \n\nFollowing the frontal passage, a surface high approaches from the \nnorthwest as we go into Thursday night through Friday morning. This \nfeature in combination with clear skies and light winds will allow \nfor ample radiational cooling to occur which will result in areas of \npatchy fog. Visibilities between 1-3 miles can be expected from the \ninner Coastal Plains around Victoria to the southern Brush Country \ncross through Alice during the early morning hours on Friday. \nConditions will improve by mid-morning hours as ample diurnal \nheating takes place. High temperatures will rebound into the lower \n70s with lows dipping into the 50s across the area with mostly clear \nskies. \n\nClouds will begin to increase from the west overnight Friday into \nSaturday with a mid-level cut off low currently over the east \nPacific amplifying and becoming a negatively-tilted trough as it \napproaches our area. Ahead of this feature, ample moisture return \nwill be ongoing across our area with PWATs between 1.5-1.8\" (greater \nthan 75th percentile). This will result in showers and thunderstorms \nacross our area throughout the day Saturday with locally heavy \nrainfall possible in the stronger cells and/or where any training \ndevelops. Medium rain chances (40-60%) will persist through Sunday \nnight with models hinting at a surface coastal trough in conjunction \nwith the mid-level trough. There are model discrepancies when it \ncomes to the exact placement and intensity of this coastal feature \nbut trends will continue to be closely monitored as we near this \nweekend.\n\nAnother cold front looks to arrive sometime Monday of next week, \nending rain chances temporarily. Low rain chances return toward the \nmiddle of next week with the return of onshore flow increasing \nmoisture.",
